# Keys permitted to sign commits on this repository.
#
# Consumed by CI (`gpg.ssh.allowedSignersFile`) so the signature check in
# quality-gates.yml verifies against a list that lives in the repo and
# changes only by reviewed pull request -- not against whatever happens
# to be on a runner or a laptop.
#
# One key per machine, never one key copied between them: a shared key
# cannot tell you which machine signed. Add a machine by adding a line
# here in the same PR that registers the key on GitHub with
# `gh ssh-key add <pub> --type signing --title "<machine> signing key"`.
#
# Every agent on a machine shares that machine's key, so a signature
# establishes "this machine, with a human present to authorise the key,
# asserts what the commit says" -- and no more. Which agent did the work
# is the `Agent:` trailer. That trailer is not a loose claim: the
# signature is computed over the whole commit object, message and
# trailers included, so altering `Agent: claude` to `Agent: grok` after
# the fact turns the signature bad (`%G?` = B). It is tamper-evident and
# human-attested. It is not independent proof that the attestation was
# truthful, and RULES.md says so rather than letting this read as more
# than it is.
#
# Remove a line the moment a machine is lost or retired. This file is
# the revocation list.

